    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d251">

                <pb facs="0281" n="1115" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/253</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schmedeman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-22T22:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 22, 1918—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 28, 9 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>485. I handed a note to the Minister for Foreign Affairs at 8.30 this evening
                    embodying substance of your telegram No. 210, January 21, 7 p.m., received at
                    6.30 o’clock. Minister for Foreign Affairs requests publication be deferred a
                    few days. He was much disturbed about publication of proposal in all its details
                    and seemed to fear difficulties from the German side if the portions of the
                    proposal affecting question of exports to Germany were published.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">10 p.m.</hi> Minister for Foreign Affairs has just
                    called and handed me a note, in reply to my note above mentioned, stating that
                    in order to avoid misunderstanding, Minister for Foreign Affairs has the <pb
                        facs="0282" n="1116" xml:id="pg1116"/> honor to say that the Norwegian
                    Government regrets it is unable for the time being to assent to the War Trade
                    Board’s proposal of December 20 to Nansen being published, but the Norwegian
                    Government cannot object to the American Government’s publishing what it has
                    proposed or offered to Norway provided that in doing so there be no publication
                    or intimation of what Norway has proposed or offered to America. The note adds
                    that the Norwegian Government hopes very soon to be able to answer the War Trade
                    Board’s proposal of December 20 and will in this connection return to the
                    question of publication.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schmedeman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
